---
// /what-we-treat/mental-health/anxiety/: What-We-Treat-Content-Briefs.md §J. Sources in
// docs/content/what-we-treat-sources-mental.md. Rotation: Reviews only. Reviewed by Dana.
import ServicePage from '../../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../../components/NextSteps.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import { WWT, CATEGORIES, MENTAL_PAGES, siblings } from '../../../data/treat.js';
import { conditionAbout } from '../../../lib/programSchema.js';

const path = '/what-we-treat/mental-health/anxiety/';

const signs = [
  'You drink or use to quiet worry, panic or social fear',
  'The relief is short, and the anxiety comes back stronger',
  'You avoid situations unless you’ve had something first',
  'A medication prescribed for anxiety has become hard to stop',
];

const treating = [
  { icon: 'shield', title: 'Skills for the moment', text: 'DBT and CBT skills give you something to do when anxiety spikes: ways to ride out the wave and question the thoughts that feed it.' },
  { icon: 'layers', title: 'The why underneath', text: 'Skills work better when you understand where the fear started. We look at the history and patterns beneath the anxiety, not just the symptom.' },
  { icon: 'chart', title: 'Progress you can measure', text: 'We track anxiety symptoms with the GAD-7 throughout treatment, and your therapist reviews your treatment plan with you every month.' },
  { icon: 'refresh', title: 'Practice in real life', text: 'You go home every day. The anxious moment at work or at the store comes back to group, where we slow it down and plan a different response.' },
];

const approaches = [
  { name: 'CBT', href: '/therapies/cbt/', text: 'Helps you notice anxious thought patterns and test them, instead of letting them run the show.' },
  { name: 'DBT', href: '/therapies/dbt/', text: 'Builds distress tolerance and emotional regulation skills for the moments when anxiety feels overwhelming.' },
  { name: 'Internal Family Systems (IFS)', href: '/therapies/internal-family-systems/', text: 'Gets to know the anxious, protective parts of you and what they are trying to guard against.' },
  { name: 'Psychodynamic therapy', href: '/therapies/inner-child-therapy/', text: 'Explores how earlier experiences and relationships may still be feeding the fear today.' },
  { name: 'Trauma-informed care', text: 'Every clinician is trauma-informed, because anxiety is often connected to older experiences of not feeling safe.' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can I keep taking Xanax or Klonopin during the program?', a: 'Sunview is abstinence-based, so benzodiazepines aren’t used during the program; anxiety is treated with therapy and psychiatric care. If you’ve taken them regularly for a long time, medically supervised detox usually comes first. Your Telemed Clinix provider reviews your other medications and makes adjustments when they’re clinically indicated.' },
  { q: 'Do you treat anxiety without substance use?', a: 'We treat anxiety when it comes with substance use, in our PHP, IOP and OP programs, with therapy and psychiatric care in one plan. If you’re looking for anxiety care on its own, we’ll help you find the right fit.' },
  { q: 'I have social anxiety. Is group therapy going to be too much?', a: 'Many people feel nervous at first. The same facilitator leads the whole session and the group stays consistent, so trust can build over time. You also meet one-on-one with your therapist every week.' },
  { q: 'How do you track whether my anxiety is improving?', a: 'We track anxiety symptoms with a standard screening questionnaire during treatment, and your therapist reviews your treatment plan and goals with you every month.' },
  { q: 'Which program should I start in?', a: 'Our Clinical Director reviews your pre-screening and recommends a level of care using ASAM criteria and clinical judgment. <a href="/programs/">Compare PHP, IOP and OP</a>.' },
];
---
<ServicePage
  pageType="MedicalWebPage"
  path={path}
  metaTitle="Anxiety and Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach | Sunview"
  description="Anxiety and panic treated alongside substance use in West Palm Beach, with therapy, psychiatric support and no benzodiazepines during the program."
  crumbs={[WWT, { name: CATEGORIES.mental.name, href: CATEGORIES.mental.href }, { name: 'Anxiety', href: path }]}
  h1="Anxiety and Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach"
  subheading="Calm that doesn’t depend on a substance, built one skill and one insight at a time."
  lead="Anxiety and panic treated alongside substance use in outpatient PHP, IOP and OP, with therapy, psychiatric support and no benzodiazepines during the program."
  faqTitle="Frequently Asked Questions About Anxiety Treatment"
  faqs={faqs}
  reviews
  about={conditionAbout('Anxiety disorders')}
>
  {/* The cycle */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The cycle</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">How Anxiety and Substance Use Feed Each Other</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Quick relief, bigger worry</p>
        <div class="prose-sv mt-6">
          <p>At Sunview, anxiety is treated as part of <a href="/what-we-treat/dual-diagnosis/">dual diagnosis treatment</a>, alongside substance use, within our Partial Hospitalization, Intensive Outpatient and Outpatient programs. Anxiety disorders are among the conditions we see most often in people who come to us for addiction treatment.</p>
          <p>Substances often start as a way to turn the volume down on worry, panic or social fear. The relief is real, but short. As it wears off, the anxiety tends to come back stronger, and the next drink or pill feels more necessary. Over time, using and anxiety keep each other going.</p>
          <p>Some people come to us after years of taking a benzodiazepine for anxiety. That’s a situation we understand well, and it usually starts with medically supervised detox. Read more about <a href="/what-we-treat/substance-use/benzodiazepines/">benzodiazepine addiction treatment</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {/* REVIEW 8.5: plain-language passage pending Elizabeth review */}
      <aside class="card self-start !p-7">
        <h3 class="text-xl">Signs the two may be connected</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          {signs.map((s) => <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check" class="mt-1 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-teal" />{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-5 border-t border-line pt-4 font-bold text-teal">Recognizing a few of these is reason enough to call. You don’t need to be sure.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Treating it at Sunview */}
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-5xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">At Sunview</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Treating Anxiety Alongside Addiction at Sunview</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Skills matter. So does where the fear began.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {treating.map((t) => (
          <div class="card">
            <Icon name={t.icon} class="h-7 w-7 text-teal" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">{t.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2">{t.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Therapies */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Therapy</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Therapy Approaches We Use</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">More than a band-aid</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">We value CBT and relapse prevention, and we teach those skills. But it’s hard to manage a trigger you don’t understand, so we also go deeper into where the anxious patterns began.</p>
        <a href="/therapies/" class="btn-teal mt-8">How therapy works at Sunview <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <dl class="divide-y divide-line self-start rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-line">
        {approaches.map((a) => (
          <div class="grid gap-1 p-6 sm:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] sm:gap-6">
            <dt class="font-extrabold">{a.html ? <Fragment set:html={a.html} /> : a.href ? <a href={a.href} class="text-teal underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-teal-light">{a.name}</a> : a.name}</dt>
            <dd>{a.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Psychiatry */}
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Medication</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Psychiatric Care and Medication</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Medication-friendly, without benzodiazepines</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">Your medications are managed by a Telemed Clinix provider as part of your program. They review what you already take, how well it works and whether anything needs to change. Appointments happen virtually from a private office at Sunview.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg">Sunview is abstinence-based, so benzodiazepines aren’t used during the program; anxiety is treated with therapy and psychiatric care. Abstinence-based doesn’t mean medication-free: your provider decides what’s clinically appropriate for you, and you can keep seeing them after you finish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card !p-8">
        <Icon name="pill" class="h-8 w-8 text-teal" />
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">What psychiatric care includes</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />Evaluation and review of your current medications</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />Appointments scheduled for you, on site</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />The same provider after discharge, if you want</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/programs/psychiatry-medication-management/" class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-teal underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-teal-light">Psychiatric care and medication management <Icon name="arrow" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextSteps
    class="section"
    title="Which Level of Care Fits"
    subtitle="Our Clinical Director helps you decide"
    level={`<p>After detox from benzodiazepines or other substances, many people start in the <a href="/programs/php/">Partial Hospitalization Program</a> for the daily structure. The <a href="/programs/iop/">Intensive Outpatient Program</a>, day or evening, fits when you need depth and have to keep working. The <a href="/programs/outpatient/">Outpatient Program</a> keeps support in place as your confidence grows.</p>`}
    related={[
      { label: 'Co-occurring mental health treatment', href: CATEGORIES.mental.href },
      ...siblings(MENTAL_PAGES, ['depression', 'trauma-ptsd']),
      { label: CATEGORIES.dual.label, href: CATEGORIES.dual.href },
    ]}
  />
</ServicePage>
